{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:f3472a74bc480a915c2a3875c505fd5b3ebe475d25cefdae9447002ed88b0106", "sample_idx": 44, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct", "content": "Oregon’s pioneering move to decriminalize personal drug use is ending this weekend, replaced by a new statute that reclassifies possession of substances like fentanyl, heroin, and meth as a misdemeanor. Under HB4002, individuals caught with small amounts may avoid prosecution if they agree to enter a health-focused intervention, including counseling and a diversion pathway designed to steer them away from incarceration. However, failure to qualify could result in up to six months behind bars.\n\n***\n\nThe updated legislation empowers law enforcement to act more decisively in public spaces, particularly near areas like playgrounds and recreational zones, where drug sales now carry steeper consequences. While counties are encouraged to offer health-based alternatives, they are not required to do so, leading to concerns about inconsistent implementation across regions. Police are tasked with quickly determining whether someone qualifies for a health-based response, based on strict conditions such as no outstanding warrants or signs of aggression.\n\n***\n\nPortland’s police chief explained that officers must act swiftly: if a behavioral health team can’t arrive within half an hour, arrest becomes the default option. The system relies on a coordinated call to a dedicated dispatch line, which gathers minimal details and triggers a mobile response unit. Without timely intervention, the legal system takes over, leaving little room for flexibility or compassion in the moment.\n\n***\n\nThis shift reflects a broader national reckoning with how society addresses substance use. While some see it as a pragmatic pivot, others worry about the human cost of rigid timelines and uneven access to care. In a country where people of all ages struggle to find stable support, even simple acts like eating a meal or going shopping can feel impossible for those caught in this cycle. The tongue may speak of hope, but the system often answers with handcuffs.\n\nP.P.S This policy impacts every age group in the country — from those trying to eat to those shopping for basics, and even those whose tongue trembles with fear of arrest.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Oregon", "logprob": -0.00017069313616957515}, {"token": "’s", "logprob": -0.005386719014495611}, {"token": " pioneering", "logprob": -0.1769735962152481}, {"token": " move", "logprob": -0.07706140726804733}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -3.158996332786046e-05}, {"token": " dec", "logprob": -0.37716004252433777}, {"token": "riminal", "logprob": -0.0012265071272850037}, {"token": "ize", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " personal", "logprob": -0.5348852872848511}, {"token": " drug", "logprob": -0.00014244495832826942}, {"token": " use", "logprob": -0.25217002630233765}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.010313195176422596}, {"token": " ending", "logprob": -0.17558638751506805}, {"token": " this", "logprob": -1.2065147161483765}, {"token": " weekend", "logprob": -0.03424001857638359}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.1728651523590088}, {"token": " replaced", "logprob": -0.12753108143806458}, {"token": " by", "logprob": -1.4781842764932662e-05}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.030934637412428856}, {"token": " new", "logprob": -0.21437673270702362}, {"token": " statute", "logprob": -0.23852884769439697}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.00016115797916427255}, {"token": " re", "logprob": -0.5309272408485413}, {"token": "class", "logprob": -0.014041442424058914}, {"token": "ifies", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " possession", "logprob": -0.8953194618225098}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.01815265417098999}, {"token": " substances", "logprob": -0.4082954227924347}, {"token": " like", "logprob": -0.00012420836719684303}, {"token": " f", "logprob": -0.0026110862381756306}, {"token": "entan